# The War Waged by the Tamil: A Chronology

| Event | Date |
|---|---:|
| Chief Minister Rajaji first mentioned introducing Hindi | 10-8-37 |
| The Madras Presidency Tamil Conference met in Tiruchirappalli and issued its final warning that Hindi was not wanted | 26-12-37 |
| The Madras Presidency Anti-Hindi Conference met in Kanchipuram and reiterated that warning | 27-2-38 |
| Hindi was introduced | 21-4-38 |
| The war council for the anti-Hindi struggle met at the Tiruchirappalli camp | 28-5-38 |
| The anti-Hindi struggle began | 3-6-38 |
| The great Tamil volunteer force set out | 1-8-38 |
| The slogan "Tamil Nadu for the Tamils" was first raised | 71-9-38 |
| Commander Annadurai was imprisoned | 26-9-38 |
| Women first entered prison | 14-11-38 |
| Leader of the struggle Periyar was imprisoned | 5-12-38 |
| Tamil hero Natarajan died | 14-1-39 |
| Tamil hero Thalamuthu died | 12-5-39 |
| Leader Periyar was released | 22-5-39 |
| Anti-Hindi volunteers received an unexpected release, first occasion | 7-6-39 |
| Anti-Hindi volunteers received an unexpected release, second occasion | 15-11-39 |
| Tamils again sounded the drum of struggle in Kanchipuram | 31-12-39 |
| Leader of the struggle Periyar issued the final warning, "If Hindi does not go, the struggle will resume" | 19-2-40 |
| Compulsory Hindi was abolished; the Tamil achieved victory | 21-2-40 |
